 <iati-activity default-currency="USD" hierarchy="1" iati-activities:version="2.03" xml:lang="EN" xmlns:iati-activities="http://d-portal.org/xmlns/iati-activities" xmlns:usg="https://explorer.usaid.gov">
  <iati-identifier>US-GOV-1-AID-523-A-13-00002</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="US-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U.S. Agency for International Development</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Capital humano</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Human Capital</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">En el marco de esta iniciativa, el socio local CIDAC analizar&#xe1; las brechas entre la oferta y la demanda de capital humano. En concreto, la iniciativa mapea las habilidades profesionales m&#xe1;s necesarias en los j&#xf3;venes por principales sectores econ&#xf3;micos; identifica brechas en la oferta laboral y de capacitaci&#xf3;n, en funci&#xf3;n de las habilidades m&#xe1;s requeridas; proporciona mejor informaci&#xf3;n a las familias, estudiantes de secundaria y universitarios, gobiernos federal y estatales y universidades sobre qu&#xe9; perfiles son m&#xe1;s demandados por los principales sectores econ&#xf3;micos; difunde resultados; lleva a cabo un estudio piloto en dos municipios y documenta las dos experiencias municipales. Se realizan actividades en Guadalajara, Ciudad de M&#xe9;xico, Monterrey, Puebla, Quer&#xe9;taro y Toluca.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under this initiative, local partner CIDAC will analyze the gaps between human capital supply and demand. Specifically, the initiative maps the most needed professional skills in young people by main economic sectors; identifies gaps in the work supply and training, based on the most required skills; provides better information to families, high school and university students, federal and state governments, and universities on what profiles are in most demand by main economic sectors; disseminates results; conducts a pilot study in two municipalities and documents the two municipal experiences. Activities are carried out in Guadalajara, Mexico City, Monterrey, Puebla, Queretaro and Toluca.</narrative>
  </description>
